e and the approximate double bottom with 2357.18, weakening the Always-In Long read and supporting a larger trading range 2357.18-2850.", "Range development: five or more further bars overlapping inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high would turn the pause into a trading range at the highs and lower Always-In relevance."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790452799999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["Bull-trend context is intact: higher swing lows 2358.62 (bar 54) to 2569.80 (bar 80) to 2641.70 (bar 86), and the 2633.31 pullback low (bar 106) is only 8.39 below 2641.70 and was reversed within one bar.", "Window net change is +7.8% (2488.82 to 2683.22) and the largest sustained leg is up (+20.8% from 2358.62 to 2850.00); the leg off 2633.31 is also up (+4.1% to 2740.42 on bar 112).", "A long range at the top of a strong bull leg is often a bull flag: price holds above the 2658.81 breakout area and above the 2633.31 range low, and there has been no bear breakout or close below the range floor.", "The 2669.67-2721.75 coil can resolve upward; a close above 2721.75 would look like trend resumption rather than range continuation."], "evidence_for": ["The last 32 bars are two-sided: breakdowns to 2648.49 (bar 101) and 2633.31 (bar 106) had no follow-through, and no bar closed above 2804.59 after the 2850.00 spike.", "Highs step down after the spike (2804.59, 2778.33, 2740.42) and the last close 2683.22 is about 5.9% below 2850.00 and below the 2718.95 midpoint of the 2633.31-2804.59 range.", "Bar 88 is a spike/climax bar (191.94-point range, 126.85-point upper tail); the 32 heavily overlapping bars after it are range behavior rather than trend follow-through.", "The final eight bars coil in a 52-point band with the smallest recent ranges, and net progress over bars 105-120 is essentially nil.", "